Z||000000||fiero56||12-07-1999||10:07 PM||||I attempted to replace my broken EGR tube from above.  Found it to be <B>impossible</B>. I screwed around with that thing for almost 3 hours last night. Today I just took off the intake plenum(red).  This may sound cheap, and I may hear about this for a while, but, can I reuse the gaskets that were on it? They appear to be in good shape. Are these things reusable or am I just better off replacing them with new ones? If I get new ones, is there anything special I should look for?||||reg||5
Z||000001||AL||12-07-1999||10:11 PM||||you might as well replace them,but i have used the same ones on my t/a and it worked fine.ital depends on $||||reg||1
Z||000002||RZURCTN||12-07-1999||10:24 PM||||If it's still in good shape, then you can try reusing it.  They aren't expensive, so replacing it would be your best bet.  Nothing special to look for, they're all pretty much the same.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||12-08-1999||07:11 AM||||I agree that they can be reused if needed but I'd replace them (hate doing things twice).<P>The plenum is under vacuum and therefore the gaskets don't see much differential pressure across the surfaces.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||12-08-1999||07:13 AM||||Also with the plenum off it is a great time to inspect all of the vacuum lines.  The small hard plastic vacuum tubing becomes brittle and easily cracks.  Just for grins it wouldn't hurt to look at each and figure what each does and maybe make a sketch of the routing.  If you have a problem later it will be easier to diagnose.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cscougar||12-08-1999||08:30 AM||||Would any of you have a diagram sketch of the routing of the vacuum hoses under the phenum? I am rebuilding a V-6 that was apart when I got it so I am confused as to the vacuum line routing.<P>Thanks,<P>Ted||||reg||5
Z||000006||fiero56||12-08-1999||08:48 AM||||I can take a picture of the hoses running around under the plenum and post it here, if it helps.  I don't think it will really show what they all connect to though, just routing.||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||12-08-1999||01:13 PM||||Check the smog sticker under the trunk lid, it will give you an idea about where the vacuum lines go!||||reg||10
